import DubC2.NuAtlas.b3_2_P2_5_Circle

/-!
# The shift-interval atlas (plan-dubC2-transform M3, T3 grades 1–2)

Generated by `DubC2/xnu.py --emit` from the exact `ν`-cell decomposition of the shift circle
(experiment X‑ν, data in `DubC2/data/transform/xnu_*.json`).  Each closed cell
`[j, j+1]/((p−q)D)` carries the certificate at its midpoint, `hullOK` over the closed cell, and the
theorem `…_cell` for **every real shift** in it (`DubC2.Gen.divisor_set_of_checked_hull`).  The
cells of the fundamental domain `[½, L/2 + ½]` are merged into closed intervals (`…_iv*`), and
`DubC2.Gen.frequently_of_circle` (period `L`, mirror `ν ↦ 1 − ν`) extends them to the circle.

* `DubC2.NuAtlas.b3_2_P2_5_iv1` — **the flagship**: `{2, 5}` is unavoidable for
  `⌊ξ(3/2)ⁿ + ν⌋` for every real `ν ∈ [½, 25/48]` and every `ξ ≠ 0` (and, by the mirror,
  on `[23/48, ½]`).
* `DubC2.NuAtlas.b3_2_P2_5_circle` — `{2, 5}` at `3/2` on the shift circle `ℝ/10ℤ`: 15 closed
  intervals, `11.85 %` of the circle, from 73 kernel-checked cells (`D ≤ 1536`).
-/
